From cf1c999c81b796b0172426049d836296bd13ea02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 16:16:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(elero): stop truncating device names at 23 bytes

Device names were stored in a 24-byte NVS field and silently cut by
strncpy when saved from the web UI. Names are UTF-8, so every umlaut
costs two bytes and a name like "Wohnzimmer Raffstore links" was cut
after saving; the cut could also land inside a multi-byte character.

- Grow the device name field to 48 bytes (47 usable). NvsDeviceConfig
  becomes 88 bytes, NVS_CONFIG_VERSION 4.
- Migrate v3 slots on restore: ESPHome preferences reject a blob whose
  size differs, so a v4 load fails on old data; the slot is then read
  through the v3 layout under the same key and rewritten as v4.
- Truncate names at a character boundary (copy_utf8_truncated), also for
  group names, which keep their 24-byte field.
- upsert_device / import_config reject an over-long name with an error
  instead of silently cutting it; the web UI caps the name input at 47
  UTF-8 bytes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019Jt9MRmy72MEcuogzanZQE
